A||||4||yobtah||Odd Noise from Getrag 5-speed...||||5||
Z||000000||yobtah||09-09-2000||03:08 PM||||I've recently noticed a faint rattling noise when I shift the car into neutral and release the clutch.  I think the same noise occurs when the car's moving, but it's harder to hear it.  If I depress the clutch, the noise stops.  I've checked fluid in the transmission... it appears full.  I think I might be hearing bearings in the transmission... is that likely?  If so, how bad is the problem?  Thanks for any help!  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||RedOktober||09-09-2000||03:45 PM||||My guess is that your noise is coming from your release bearing( throw out bearing). especially if the noise goes away if you push on the clutch.  You could have also broken a spring on the clutch disk. Either way, tranny has to come out if you want it fixed properly. <BR> Good luck, Hopefully I'm wrong.<P>------------------<BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater)||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||09-09-2000||06:34 PM||||It sounds like the throw out bearing or the input shaft bearing (what the release bearing rides on).  Hopefully it isn't the input bearing....they're a bear to install (must "crack" the case and press it in from the inside).<P>||||reg||10
Z||000003||loafer87gt||09-09-2000||09:24 PM||||I think I know what sound your talking about, kinda like plastic gears clattering together. I took my car to the GM dealership when I noticed the sound and they told me it was a problem with the gears in the transmission. I guess the MG-282 that is in the Fiero and a couple of other GM cars has a problem with some sort of coating wearing off the gears, resulting in the clattering sound. There is actually a service bulletin for the problem, and it recommends that you use GM Synchoromesh transmission fluid to quieten down the sound. I think I also recall that if the synchromesh fluid didn't fix the problem, that adding an additive called "Extend" will further quiet things up, BUT be sure to call your dealer to confirm that this is the right additive to use. Call your GM dealer and ask him about the problem, and they should be able to get you the part numbers for the tranny fluid and the additive.||||reg||1
Z||000004||CW85T-Type||09-10-2000||02:22 AM||||I am currently going throgh the advanced stage of what yers is doing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Mine made that noise for about 6K miles and then all the sudden one day getting of the freway somthing let loose.  I am *ASS*uming that it is the input shaft because the clutch feel like it is working, but I can shift gears with the clutch engaged and not go anywhere :P  There was no "clutch burning smell" like it was the clutch slipping and going out.<P>It looks like a helluva lot of work to change the tranny, but I'm doing it anyways  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  i'm putting a 5spd 4-cyl unit in, replacing the dead 4spd 6-cyl one.<P>Chris<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2m6||||reg||11
